        "name": "Escaping",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The term is URL-encoded with urllib.parse.quote(term, safe=\"\"), so &, =, \", <, > and spaces are all percent-encoded inside the href; the resulting URL is passed through html.escape, and the visible text uses html.escape(term) (quote=True by default), so neither `\"><script>x</script>` nor `a&b=c` can break out of the attribute or the text."
